{"spec_element": "invariant",
 "proof_obligation": "bridge",
 "diagnosis": "The second loop (copying y into b) has no invariant tracking which elements of y have been copied into b. After the loop, Dafny only knows 0 <= i <= y.Length and 0 <= index <= sumi, but cannot relate the contents of b[x.Length..] to y[..]. Without an invariant like b[..index] == x[..] + y[..i], the loop exit condition (i == y.Length) and invariants cannot imply the postcondition b[..] == x[..] + y[..]. Additionally, the first loop lacks an explicit invariant index == i, which is needed to reason about the relationship between index and i at loop exit."}

